  "track.fp.preset.pure": "Functional programming · pure functions and the substitution model",
  "track.fp.m.pure.title": "fee() reading today's date, or fee(date) taking the date",
  "track.fp.m.pure.overview": "The ClinicBook visit fee: 200,000 VND on weekdays, 300,000 VND on Saturday and Sunday. First version: fee() reads today's date itself and counts its calls. Second version: fee(date) takes the date as a parameter. For each, replace every expression with its value (the substitution model), then run the same test on each day of the week of 23–29 November 2026.",
  "track.fp.m.pure.wrapup": "fee() reads today's date and bumps a counter. The substitution table stops at once: the same expression has two values, and extracting a variable changes the counter. The test is green on Monday and red on Saturday and Sunday though nobody touched the code. fee(date) takes the date as a parameter: every row substitutes, reducing to 600_000; the tests pass fixed dates, so they are green every day. The clock and the counter are still there, but in the calling layer, where everyone can see them.",
  "track.fp.m.pure.simp.1": "The fee has only two levels and no public holidays; the week of 23–29 November 2026 is the real calendar, the amounts are the site's. The substitution table records only the relevant substitutions; constant reductions such as SATURDAY == SATURDAY are merged.",
  "track.fp.m.pure.simp.2": "Carli's definition of a pure function (two conditions) and that of Vermeulen and co-authors (referential transparency) are two ways of saying the same thing; Seemann calls it a deterministic query without side effects.",
  "track.fp.m.pure.ctl.hint": "Switch the version and walk again; compare the substitution table (red rows cannot be substituted) and the test row by day.",
  "track.fp.m.pure.ctl.case": "Version",
  "track.fp.m.pure.ctl.case.impure": "fee() reads today's date",
  "track.fp.m.pure.ctl.case.pure": "fee(date) takes the date",
  "track.fp.m.pure.diagramTitle": "The outside world, the call, the value, the test",
  "track.fp.m.pure.diagramDesc": "What the call's result depends on, and what the test sees",
  "track.fp.m.pure.n.world": "Clock and counter",
  "track.fp.m.pure.n.call": "The fee call",
  "track.fp.m.pure.n.value": "Value",
  "track.fp.m.pure.n.test": "Tests",
  "track.fp.m.pure.met.subst": "Substitutable rows",
  "track.fp.m.pure.met.opaque": "Rows that cannot be substituted",
  "track.fp.m.pure.met.red": "Days with a red test",
  "track.fp.cap.pure": "The clock and the counter feed the call; the call yields a value; the test checks the value. A red node is where the result depends on something other than the input.",
  "track.fp.m.pure.s.impure.s1.title": "Replace fee() with its value",
  "track.fp.m.pure.s.impure.s1.explain": "The program: total = fee() + fee(). Try replacing fee() with its result: run on Monday 23 November it gives 200_000, run on Saturday 28 November it gives 300_000. One expression, two values: there is no value to substitute. fee() is not referentially transparent.",
  "track.fp.m.pure.ev.impure.s1": "Replace fee() with its value",
  "track.fp.m.pure.s.impure.s2.title": "Extract a variable: val a = fee(); total = a + a",
  "track.fp.m.pure.s.impure.s2.explain": "For a pure function the two forms are the same. Here fee() also bumps calls: fee() + fee() adds 2, the extracted variable adds 1. The fee lookup count in the analytics changes because of a tiny refactoring.",
  "track.fp.m.pure.ev.impure.s2": "Extract a variable: val a = fee(); total = a + a",
  "track.fp.m.pure.s.impure.s3.title": "Run the test on Monday: green",
  "track.fp.m.pure.s.impure.s3.explain": "weekdayFee checks fee() == 200_000. Run on the dev machine on Monday 23 November: green. The test does not say which day it checks; the day lives in the clock of the machine running it.",
  "track.fp.m.pure.ev.impure.s3": "Run the test on Monday: green",
  "track.fp.m.pure.s.impure.s4.title": "CI runs on Saturday 28 November: red",
  "track.fp.m.pure.s.impure.s4.explain": "Saturday's nightly build reruns the same test with no line changed: fee() returns 300_000 and the test is red. Run all week, it is red on exactly two days, Saturday and Sunday. The test flips with the calendar.",
  "track.fp.m.pure.ev.impure.s4": "CI runs on Saturday 28 November: red",
  "track.fp.m.pure.s.pure.s1.title": "Replace d with its value",
  "track.fp.m.pure.s.pure.s1.explain": "fee takes the date as a parameter. d is LocalDate.of(2026, 11, 28), a Saturday; substitute d: total = fee(2026-11-28) + fee(2026-11-28). Nothing but the parameter decides the result.",
  "track.fp.m.pure.ev.pure.s1": "Replace d with its value",
  "track.fp.m.pure.s.pure.s2.title": "Substitute the body, reduce to one value",
  "track.fp.m.pure.s.pure.s2.explain": "Replace each call with the function body: 28 November is a Saturday, so the condition is true, each call becomes 300_000 and total becomes 600_000. Extracting val a = fee(d); a + a also gives 600_000: the two forms are one program.",
  "track.fp.m.pure.ev.pure.s2": "Substitute the body, reduce to one value",
  "track.fp.m.pure.s.pure.s3.title": "Tests with fixed dates: green",
  "track.fp.m.pure.s.pure.s3.explain": "Two tests pass the date in: Monday 23 November gives 200_000, Saturday 28 November gives 300_000. Run on Monday: green. There is now a test for the weekend too, which the old test could not have.",
  "track.fp.m.pure.ev.pure.s3": "Tests with fixed dates: green",
  "track.fp.m.pure.s.pure.s4.title": "The shell reads the clock; tests are green every day",
  "track.fp.m.pure.s.pure.s4.explain": "Reading LocalDate.now(clock) and counting for analytics move to the layer that calls fee, at the edge of the app. Run the tests all week: no red day, because the tests no longer read the clock. The side effects do not vanish; they just move outwards (chapter K9).",
  "track.fp.m.pure.ev.pure.s4": "The shell reads the clock; tests are green every day",
  "track.fp.m.pure.co.try": "Watch the substitution table: a red row is where replacing an expression with its value changes the program.",
  "track.fp.m.pure.co.impure.s2": "Carli (ch.3): twiceAndLog returns x * 2 just like twice but also prints a line; replacing the call with its result loses the line, so it is not pure. The counter here is the same. [[src:book-fp-tut]]",
  "track.fp.m.pure.co.impure.s3": "Seemann (13.1.3): queries must be deterministic: no random numbers, GUIDs, time of day or day of the month. [[src:book-seemann]]",
  "track.fp.m.pure.co.impure.s4": "A test that depends on the day it runs is not deterministic: the same code, different results. The fix is not rerunning until green but moving the clock out of the function under test.",
  "track.fp.m.pure.co.pure.s1": "Vermeulen and co-authors (ch.1): an expression is referentially transparent if, in every program, replacing it with its result leaves the meaning unchanged; a function is pure if f(x) is so for every such x. [[src:book-fp-manning]]",
  "track.fp.m.pure.co.pure.s2": "Vermeulen and co-authors (ch.1): when every expression is substitutable, we reason as if solving an equation, replacing equals with equals down to the simplest form. That is the substitution model. [[src:book-fp-manning]]",
  "track.fp.m.pure.co.pure.s3": "Seemann (13.1.3): a pure function call can be replaced by its result; once it returns, the result is all you need to care about. [[src:book-seemann]]",
  "track.fp.m.pure.co.pure.s4": "Seemann (8.2.2): WillAccept takes now as a parameter, and the controller passes DateTime.Now in. Vermeulen and co-authors call this layout a pure core with a thin outer layer that handles effects. [[src:book-seemann]] [[src:book-fp-manning]]",
  "track.fp.vz.tab.pure": "Substitution table",
