  "track.fp.m.persist.met.depth": "Deepest stack",
  "track.fp.cap.persist": "Top: the selected list points into the original. Bottom: the fee sum uses the thread stack. A red node: the original changed by accident, or the stack deep enough to overflow.",
  "track.fp.m.persist.s.mutable.s1.title": "Add b4 through selected = booked",
  "track.fp.m.persist.s.mutable.s1.explain": "The picker screen writes val selected = booked, then selected.add(b4). val only fixes the name; it does not make the object immutable: both names point to the same MutableList, so booked gets b4 too. No new node is created, and that is exactly the problem.",
  "track.fp.m.persist.ev.mutable.s1": "Add b4 through selected = booked",
  "track.fp.m.persist.s.mutable.s2.title": "Drop the first booking of selected",
  "track.fp.m.persist.s.mutable.s2.explain": "selected.removeAt(0) drops b1. Since it is one object, the booked list loses b1 as well: both changes made through selected leak into booked.",
  "track.fp.m.persist.ev.mutable.s2": "Drop the first booking of selected",
  "track.fp.m.persist.s.persistent.s1.title": "Add b4 at the front: Cons(b4, booked)",
  "track.fp.m.persist.s.persistent.s1.explain": "Exactly 1 new node is created; its tail is booked itself (checked with ===), so the 3 old nodes are shared, not copied. booked is still b1, b2, b3.",
  "track.fp.m.persist.ev.persistent.s1": "Add b4 at the front: Cons(b4, booked)",
  "track.fp.m.persist.s.persistent.s2.title": "Drop the first element: selected.tail",
  "track.fp.m.persist.s.persistent.s2.explain": "Dropping the first element returns the tail: 0 new nodes, and the result is booked itself. Nothing is deleted; every old version stays usable, which is why the structure is called persistent.",
  "track.fp.m.persist.ev.persistent.s2": "Drop the first element: selected.tail",
  "track.fp.m.persist.s.plain.s3.title": "Summing 50,000 fees: descending frame by frame",
  "track.fp.m.persist.s.plain.s3.explain": "total(xs) = xs.head.fee + total(xs.tail): the addition can only happen after the inner call returns, so each element holds a frame on the stack. After 5,000 elements: 5,001 frames waiting.",
  "track.fp.m.persist.ev.plain.s3": "Summing 50,000 fees: descending frame by frame",
  "track.fp.m.persist.s.plain.s4.title": "Element 10,000: StackOverflowError",
  "track.fp.m.persist.s.plain.s4.explain": "The depth passes the illustrative limit of 10,000 frames: the app crashes before a single addition is done. A monthly report has only a few hundred bookings and runs fine; the bug only shows with a whole year of data.",
  "track.fp.m.persist.ev.plain.s4": "Element 10,000: StackOverflowError",
  "track.fp.m.persist.s.tailrec.s3.title": "An accumulator and tailrec: one frame",
  "track.fp.m.persist.s.tailrec.s3.explain": "total(xs.tail, acc + xs.head.fee): the call is the last thing done; nothing is left once it returns. With tailrec the compiler turns the recursion into a loop: the depth is always 1.",
  "track.fp.m.persist.ev.tailrec.s3": "An accumulator and tailrec: one frame",
  "track.fp.m.persist.s.tailrec.s4.title": "All 50,000 elements: 10,000,000,000 VND",
  "track.fp.m.persist.s.tailrec.s4.explain": "The depth stays 1 at every mark; the total is 50,000 × 200,000 VND = 10,000,000,000 VND. On an ordinary Kotlin List, xs.sumOf { it.fee } gives the same result and already runs as a loop.",
  "track.fp.m.persist.ev.tailrec.s4": "All 50,000 elements: 10,000,000,000 VND",
  "track.fp.m.persist.co.try": "Two independent controls: steps 1–2 watch the list table, steps 3–4 the stack depth table.",
  "track.fp.m.persist.co.mutable.s2": "Carli (ch.6): immutable is not constant. A name declared with val cannot be reassigned, yet the object it points to can still change if its type allows. Kotlin's read-only List is not immutable either (Kotlin track, chapter K7). [[src:book-fp-tut]]",
  "track.fp.m.persist.co.persistent.s1": "Vermeulen and co-authors (3.3): adding an element to the front of xs returns Cons(x, xs); since the list is immutable, xs need not be copied but is simply reused. That is data sharing. [[src:book-fp-manning]]",
  "track.fp.m.persist.co.persistent.s2": "Vermeulen and co-authors (3.3): dropping the first element returns the tail; the original list stays intact. Carli (ch.7) separates three words: immutable (unchanged after creation), functional (handled only with pure functions), persistent (always keeps the previous version). [[src:book-fp-manning]] [[src:book-fp-tut]]",
  "track.fp.m.persist.co.plain.s3": "Vermeulen and co-authors (ch.2): a call is in tail position when the caller does nothing but return its result. 1 + go(...) is not, because the addition remains. [[src:book-fp-manning]]",
  "track.fp.m.persist.co.plain.s4": "Vermeulen and co-authors (Exercise 3.9): foldRight written with plain recursion is not stack-safe and throws StackOverflowError on large lists; foldLeft written with tailrec is. [[src:book-fp-manning]]",
  "track.fp.m.persist.co.tailrec.s3": "Kotlin docs: tailrec applies only when the function calls itself as its final operation; not when code follows the call, inside try/catch/finally, or for open functions. When the conditions hold, the compiler removes the recursion and leaves a loop. [[src:kt-functions]]",
  "track.fp.m.persist.co.tailrec.s4": "Carli (ch.6): the decompiled tailrec function is a while(true) loop with no recursive call left. Without tailrec the compiler does not do this on its own, even when the call is in tail position (Vermeulen and co-authors, ch.2). [[src:book-fp-tut]] [[src:book-fp-manning]]",
  "track.fp.vz.tab.persist": "List nodes and stack depth",
  "track.fp.vz.persist.cap": "Each cell is a list node. Outlined: a node just created or added. Bold: a node shared with booked. Red hatched: booked changed by accident.",
  "track.fp.vz.persist.scap": "Stack depth by elements visited among {n} bookings. Illustrative limit: {lim} frames.",
  "track.fp.vz.persist.legend": "\"?\": that step has not come yet. Red: deeper than half the limit, or an overflow. Bold: 1 frame (now a loop).",
